HST Office: Windows - list and use signing certificates whose key lives in a legacy CryptoAPI CSP.

USB tokens of the Vietnamese CAs (VNPT-CA "Ace PKI Token CSP v1.0" and other CSP-only middleware)
register their certificates in CurrentUser\My with a key provider info that names a CryptoAPI
CSP, but ship no CNG key storage provider and no smart card minidriver. Upstream Windows signing
is CNG-only (CRYPT_ACQUIRE_ONLY_NCRYPT_KEY_FLAG in the certificate list, the PDF signer and xmlsec
mscng), so CryptAcquireCertificatePrivateKey fails with NTE_NOT_FOUND and the "Select
certificate" dialog is empty although the token is plugged in and its certificates are in the
user store.

- xmlsecurity (mscrypt): a certificate counts as personal when CNG opens its key (unchanged) or
  when its key provider info names an installed CryptoAPI CSP. The CSP case is decided from the
  property alone: listing never opens the token or asks for a PIN.
- svl (PDF signing): CRYPT_ACQUIRE_PREFER_NCRYPT_KEY_FLAG: CNG first, then the CSP handle, which
  CryptMsg accepts with its AT_SIGNATURE / AT_KEYEXCHANGE key spec.
- xmlsec mscng (ODF / OOXML signing): when CNG cannot open the key, acquire it through CryptoAPI
  and sign RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 hashes with CryptSignHash (signature byte order reversed).

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0; xmlsec: MIT).
Test: needs a Windows build and a CSP-only token (not covered by the SoftHSM2 test).
